    "notes": {
        "WFPC2": "2026-11-05: blur set to 0 by hand after the auto-calibration disagreed with itself. F606W pass-1 chi^2 residual 0.753 det px rested on 5 marginal stars with a FLAT chi^2 landscape (flat-topped WFPC2 cores); applied to the twins it produced a 2.2x peak-flux deficit vs the real stars (median peak_frac 0.022 vs 0.051). At blur 0 the 22 S/N>=100 stars prefer no extra blur (FWHM ratios 0.51-0.84 i.e. real stars NARROWER than the model, peak-frac ratio 1.40 +/- 0.5): the MAST-DB model runs slightly wide for some fields, which is a model-error matter for psf_err, not fixable by blur>=0. F814W rested on 1 star. Revisit with a peak-flux-based calibrator if WFPC2 model width becomes a science question. 2026-11-09 follow-up: the width-SCALE alternative (option 4) was measured on the star-check crops and REJECTED -- per-star best scales scatter 0.3-1.2 with no global value that helps (median chi2(s)/chi2(1) 0.97 at any s in 0.5-0.8, 16-84% spanning 0.74-2.05; the mismatch is per-field focus/breathing SHAPE, not a coherent width). The err_frac ~4.9 F606W map was then traced to 3 outlier stars (J0819+4534, J1153+4612, J1405+5243; error_map_pool_outliers) and the pool-cleaned map reads 0.041, in line with F814W 0.035. The blur veto stands; WFPC2 model error ships as the cleaned model_vs_stars map. 2026-11-10 CORRECTION: the \"scale rejected\" conclusion above was drawn on a corrupted pool -- 15 of 26 F606W star-check records had twin crops miscut by 1-12 px (edge/lattice-mismatch stars; the miscut records were also the flat-chi^2-landscape evidence and the 4.9-map outliers). On well-centred pairs (guards now in band() and load_checks) the scale fit is tight: F606W 0.832, applied as width_scale (PSFSCALE) to every WFPC2 F606W kernel; residual after rebuild 0.967 (scatter 0.87-1.04), the field-to-field part left to the error map. The blur veto itself stands (a blur cannot shrink).",
        "WFPC2_F450W": "2026-11-18: re-derived at S/N>=20 (2 stars, both J0820+4847: 0.721/0.883, median 0.80; supersedes the S/N>=50 n=1 value 0.7207). The correction is real and larger than F606W/F814W (0.9448/0.9445) because the F450W DB ePSF is built from only 39 stars: its azimuthal wing is ~2x the F606W ePSF wing relative to peak at r=2-7 native px (the 94-131-star builds sit close to physical), i.e. the small-sample build leaves noisy, elevated wings. The bulk of all 7 checked stars (S/N 7-164) reads 0.62-0.83, consistent. If more F450W fields with stars arrive, re-derive."
    },
